    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d470">

                <pb facs="0577" n="319" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 195.1/316</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Mr.</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#italic">J. H. Morrison</hi>
                    
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 4, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received, by reference
                    from the White House, your letter to the President of January 26, 1915, wherein
                    you urge that it is a serious mistake to permit the sailing of the steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dacia.</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d470-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>In reply you are advised that the Department does not perceive in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dacia</hi> case any serious complications involving the
                    Government of the United States.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d470-f1" n="1" xml:id="d470-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. Correspondence regarding the transfer of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dacia</hi> to the American flag and her contemplated voyage is printed in
                    the section relating to transfer of ships, <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>,
                        <ref target="#pg674">p. 674</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
